Yeah, we do have an iMac, a home iMac, and so if you're going to go that route, it's like you still have to have an amazing product because that's what actually generates the word of mouth that generates it.

287
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:31,680
I mean, so much of what you've been talking about is like having that core product, the core brand, and that's how it actually pays off.

288
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:32,480
So yeah.

289
00:28:33,040 --> 00:28:41,120
And it's been interesting for B2B to B2C, we're really focused on people like B2C, like making sure we have the best possible app that people love it.

290
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:44,240
And it turns out a lot of students are using the app and actually love it on their own.

291
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:48,640
And again, it's not something that people tell them to do or their parents or their school, they use it on their own.

292
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:52,960
But we're also happy to have this natural extension of working with schools.

293
00:28:53,120 --> 00:29:03,840
But for me, the compass is always how do we build the best possible experience for the user, make it fun, make it motivating, make it as easy to use as possible.

294
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:11,360
And so as long as we do that, we'll still be able to make sure that the next generation wants to use the app as well.

