00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:47,440
What are some of the key things that you think make the OPAL brand, the touches in the app, the name itself, the design, the feel?

332
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:54,880
Like, you know, how do you classify or quantify brand for Opel?

333
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:56,880
Yeah, I mean, there's a lot of things.

334
00:33:57,120 --> 00:34:03,040
You know, we the company started with a manifesto actually that I wrote before, like, building a product.

335
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:07,120
It was really more like thinking about, you know, what is, what is going on here?

336
00:34:07,280 --> 00:34:14,080
You know, we've got trillion dollar companies and they're selling people's attention and they've built this technology that everybody uses every single day.

337
00:34:14,640 --> 00:34:25,120
Technology is really good, but because of this business model and because of the companies they're building the technology used by people, we have the outcomes that we we know, which is overuse of screens.

338
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:38,800
So the manifest is basically saying, we can change this and we can actually design products differently to benefit of all the great stuff that technology brings to people, all the good stuff, but also like read out the bad.

339
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:43,200
And so we kind of started with that and then the product was kind of a consequence of that.

340
00:34:43,680 --> 00:34:47,600
And yeah, the name is an important part of our story.

341
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,200
Opal is a gemstone.

342
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:53,600
That's why you get all these gemstones inside the app, internal marketing as well.

343
00:34:54,800 --> 00:35:06,560
And Opal is actually also the reason they chose this name is that., you know, it was striking to me that phones are basically something that you touch all day, every day, hundreds of times per day.

344
00:35:07,680 --> 00:35:09,440
And so, you know, what are phones?

345
00:35:09,680 --> 00:35:20,720
Phones are made of basically glass, aluminum, all sorts of different kinds of components, and they're electrically charged, they tend to be warm because of what's going on in it.

346
00:35:20,880 --> 00:35:24,960
And so I was thinking about that, what is the exact opposite, you know, from a tactile perspective to a phone?

347
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:27,760
And that's where, you know, gemstone kind of came up.

348
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:32,960
I mean, opal in particular, opal is a gemstone that's set to calm the mind in particular.

349
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:35,520
In particular, blue opal, it comes in different variations.

350
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:37,760
So, and it's also very, very precious gemstones.

351
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:39,920
That's the reason why, you know, the name happened.

352
00:35:40,080 --> 00:35:40,880
So it's not random.

353
00:35:41,040 --> 00:35:42,960
There's a real reason why it's opal.

354
00:35:43,440 --> 00:35:56,320
And then, you know, the whole product experience is centered around the fact that the more you focus, the more you kind of unlock these opal gemstones with different colors and different shapes.

355
00:35:56,480 --> 00:36:06,240
And we put a lot of effort to kind of basically, it's a constant debate in our team to basically make sure that the whole experience revolves around around these gemstones.

356
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:33,680
And so that's, that's, obviously, one of the things., the most loved interaction in the app, which sounds completely stupid, but the most loved interaction is that unlocking of that stone, like when you get granted that's that new gemstone because you've you've passed a new milestone, you've used the app for a certain amount of days, for example, you get to kind of tap to crack the gemstone and that's the most loved interaction.

357
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:41,440
And people really remember this, talk about it and really helps build the brand because this is what the kind of things that people remember.

358
00:36:42,080 --> 00:36:43,120
You know, another example is.

